pi.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is really great!! Thanks! I believe this would be extremely valuable to developers and it would be great to have this for 4.7.\n\nI haven't tested this as thoroughly as I normally would, but this seems like something that's pretty simple and will be easy to bug fix if there are any edge cases that are discovered after merging.\n\nI've left a couple of comments about the documentation and signal/constant naming.\n\n> No idea if there's a necessity for having the signal/notification.\n\n@bruvzg Currently the developer must poll this value every frame, even though it may never change (if the player is using an SDR screen or an HDR screen that has a stable brightness setting). An example of the current approach is shown in the documentation here: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/rendering/hdr_output.html#using-output-max-linear-value\n\nSo I think the signal is valuable in addition to the other events?? You might want to hook a shader uniform up to this value... does a signal help with this? I really am not the one to make the call on this, so if someone else wants to jump in who is more well versed in what justifies a signal and what doesn't, please do so.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#pullrequestreview-3946504468","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666","author_ass